{
  "_comment": [
    "Demo dataset for `task local:demo:*` and `task cloud:demo:*` (issue #356).",
    "",
    "This file is the ONLY home for the demo's names, amounts and counts. scripts/demo/demo.sh",
    "contains no literal endpoint, amount or count — everything it needs is either here or",
    "resolved at runtime from the environment.",
    "",
    "Two resolver forms are understood inside `payload`, `evidence` and `facts`:",
    "  {\"@threshold\": \"<name>\", \"@delta\": <number>}  -> the LIVE value of that authority-policy",
    "      threshold (from GET /api/authority/policy) plus @delta. Nothing here restates a",
    "      threshold; if the policy changes, the demo data follows it.",
    "  {\"@ref\": \"<key>\"}  -> a value discovered during seeding (a real account id, a real",
    "      scored-transaction id, and so on). Never a made-up identifier.",
    "",
    "The seed password is a KNOWN THROWAWAY for a demo environment and is overridable with the",
    "environment variable named in credentials.passwordEnv. It grants nothing outside a demo",
    "cluster that is rebuilt on demand."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "targets": {
    "local": {
      "description": "docker-compose gateway (infra/local/gateway.nginx.conf).",
      "baseUrlEnv": "DEMO_BASE_URL",
      "baseUrlDefault": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    "cloud": {
      "description": "AKS istio ingress. The host is READ from the cluster, never baked in.",
      "baseUrlEnv": "DEMO_BASE_URL",
      "baseUrlDefault": null,
      "hostFromEnv": "CUSTOM_DOMAIN",
      "hostFromKubectl": {
        "resource": "gateway",
        "name": "banking-demo-gateway",
        "namespace": "aks-istio-ingress",
        "jsonpath": "{.spec.servers[*].hosts[*]}"
      },
      "scheme": "https"
    }
  },
  "credentials": {
    "passwordEnv": "DEMO_SEED_PASSWORD",
    "passwordDefault": "Copilot-Phase3-Verify!2026"
  },
  "emailDomain": "banking-demo.com",
  "_identityComment": [
    "ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. user-service auto-promotes the FIRST account registered in an empty",
    "environment to admin (UserService.CreateUserAsync). So the admin identity is registered",
    "first and DELIBERATELY absorbs that rule; every other role is then granted explicitly via",
    "POST /api/admin/promote with the admin token. Nothing here relies on bootstrap-at-startup",
    "seeding, which never promotes accounts created after the service came up."
  ],
